{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463641-would-it-be-impossible-to-play-a-chorister-polytheist","id":1463641,"title":"Would it be impossible to play a chorister polytheist?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-12T19:53:01-07:00","id":1463641,"title":"Would it be impossible to play a chorister polytheist?","content":"so like,the choristers are defined by their monotheism,yes? They might follow Jesus,Krishna,Even Mithras. But they follow only one god,would it be impossible for one of them to follow an entire pantheons,be it greek,aztec,slavic,chinese etc... as aspects of one god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T21:19:07-07:00","id":1463646,"title":"","content":"Are Angels the equivalent of lesser gods? Christians pray to Angels and Saints. Seems like a pantheon to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-13-2021, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T21:46:28-07:00","id":1463647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463641-would-it-be-impossible-to-play-a-chorister-polytheist?p=1463646#post1463646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Angels the equivalent of lesser gods? Christians prey to Angels and Saints. Seems like a pantheon to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's a good point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T21:58:45-07:00","id":1463648,"title":"","content":"Choristers generally come from monotheistic backgrounds, but the Tradition promotes the idea of &quot;The One&quot; which is a more universalist approach to a singular supreme deity that allows multiple faith traditions to coexist by seeing any method of honoring The One through human religious practices is valid.<br /> <br /> So, it somewhat depends on what sort of polytheist you're looking for. Worshiping multiple gods would be out of keeping with the Tradition's conceptualization of The One. In many ways the Chorus is quasi-Henotheistic as it is. So a Henotheistic take of one supreme deity that you worship, but multiple lesser deities you honor according to their station works just fine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T02:58:09-07:00","id":1463674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463641-would-it-be-impossible-to-play-a-chorister-polytheist?p=1463646#post1463646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Angels the equivalent of lesser gods? Christians prey to Angels and Saints. Seems like a pantheon to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that the comparison doesn't work from an outsiders perspective, but the Chorus are exactly the kind of people who are going to violently disagree with that comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:05:56-07:00","id":1463675,"title":"","content":"Soft polytheists certainly. Hindus, neoplatonics and a lot of Buddhist traditions spring to mind. After all the One speaks in many voices. In Revised one of their npcs is a noted shintoist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T05:27:56-07:00","id":1463695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463641-would-it-be-impossible-to-play-a-chorister-polytheist?p=1463646#post1463646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Angels the equivalent of lesser gods? Christians prey to Angels and Saints. Seems like a pantheon to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very finicky area that heavily depends on what you mean by pray. Those denominations that do pray to saints are praying to them for intercession, which is a very different thing than worship. The saints certainly aren't considered gods, neither are the angels. So we'd need to know more to see whether this counts for the OPs purposes. I suspect not.<br /> <br /> Of course the Chorus is not bound by anything like that, so if anyone wants to make a Chorister who considers the angels lesser gods have at it.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the term for belief in a single supreme deity with the possibility of other lesser deities is called Henotheism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T05:42:55-07:00","id":1463698,"title":"","content":"Any polytheism you end up with will be couched in monotheistic (or henotheistic) terms. It's like asking if you can be an Etherite who practices magic: technically, yes; you can. Such an Etherite is called a scientific mystic. She might be attempting to revitalize sciences such as alchemy or astrology, for instance; or she might even be attempting to turn the sorts of \u201cmagic circles\u201d that are normally the purview of the Hermetics into a science. To an outsider, she's a mystic. But she herself doesn't see what she does as mysticism; she's exploring the <i>scientific principles</i> behind these things. <br /> <br /> In a similar way, a Chorister might harbor beliefs that, to an outsider, don't seem particularly monotheistic. But if you ask <i>him</i> to explain it to you, you'll find his explanation to be rooted in monotheistic terms. Sure, he venerates the celestial deities of the planets: Luna, Mercury, Venus, Solis, Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn; but he's careful to point out that they're Pure Ones, and servants/manifestations of the One, the Supreme Being who rules over all. <br /> <br /> (I recently read a book called \u201cPlanet Narnia\u201d, which argued that the famous Christian apologist C.S.Lewis wrote each of the books in the Chronicles of Narnia to illustrate the character of an astrological planet, and that Aslan represents a different one of these in each book: Jupiter in \u201cThe Lion, the Witch, and the Wardrobe\u201d, Mars in \u201cPrince Caspian\u201d, Solis in \u201cThe Voyage of the Dawn Treader\u201d, Luna in \u201cThe Silver Chair\u201d, Mercury in \u201cThe Horse and His Boy\u201d, Venus in \u201cThe Magician's Nephew\u201d, and Saturn in \u201cThe Last Battle\u201d. I could see a fictionalized version of Lewis, as presented in said book, as a Chorister.)<br /> <br /> What you <i>won't</i> find in the Celestial Chorus, at least not in good standing, is someone who flat-out denies that there <i>is</i> a Supreme Being. Hardcore atheists or polytheists don't fit. But an \u201catheist\u201d who believes in a Supreme One who takes a mostly hands-off approach to day to day life, or a \u201cpolytheist\u201d who views her pantheon of gods as servants or manifestations of a higher power? They're not your <i>typical</i> Chorister; but they still believe in the One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-13-2021, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T13:18:35-07:00","id":1463744,"title":"","content":"Neo-Platonists held that all the gods were but aspects of the True God. Thus Neo-Platonists could worship the entire Greek, Egyptian, and Roman pantheons plus many other gods too and they were strictly monotheistic. This may seem odd, but as someone brought up as a Christian and who attended Sunday school, it's no different than the Trinity. &quot;The three are one, and the one is three.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T18:36:35-07:00","id":1463769,"title":"","content":"This isn't that uncommon a view.<br /> <br /> Most real theological interpretations of the Chinese Celestial Bureaucracy had the many gods as emanations of Heaven, the pure essence of creation. When Heaven is referred to as an individual personality, it is the Jade Emperor, but most references are just to <i>T\u00ecan</i> (heaven), <i>D\u00ec</i> (God) or <i>Sh\u00ecangd\u00ec</i> (Highest Deity), by themselves or in compositions that refer to an aspect of Heaven.<br /> <br /> Hinduism frequently have the same characteristic, with its many deities being emanations of the One, and even when it isn't the default view of a given religion it isn't too hard to find theologians in that religions that do interpret things as such.<br /> <br /> Now, there is a difference between the view of many gods as emanations of the One or as its servants. I think it likely that the second case is less common at the Chorus, and possibly leads to heated debate, but both should be found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T19:23:15-07:00","id":1463775,"title":"","content":"I would say that \u201cmany gods as servants of the One\u201d would tend to be thought of as \u201cangels or angel-like\u201d. Going back to C.S.Lewis, his Ransom Trilogy (\u201cOut of the Silent Planet\u201d, \u201cPerelandra\u201d, and \u201cThat Hideous Strength\u201d) featured Eldil and Oyarsa, which drew comparisons to angels. But the Oyarsa we're also, in effect, pseudo-greek gods: Malachandra was Mars, Perelandra was Venus, Viritrilbia was Mercury, Glundandra was Jupiter, Lurgandra was Saturn. (Did I mention Lewis's fascination with astrology?) So you have \u201carchangels of the planets\u201d with characteristics similar to Roman deities. In a similar way, I could easily see at least part of the Celestial Bureaucracy bring thought of largely as \u201cvariant angels\u201d by a Chinese Chorister. <br /> <br /> That, and bear in mind that while these \u201cpseudo-pantheists\u201d <i>do</i> exist in the Celestial Chorus, they're a minority; and if you want to play something like that, you should put some serious thought into whether the Celestial Chorus is the right faction for your character, and why. What about the Chorister mindset speaks to you? Or are you just doing this to subvert expectations, with the main thing that you like about a polytheistic Chorister being that she <i>isn't</i> like the rest of the Chorus? Because of it's the latter, you're doing the Chorus a disservice. <br /> <br /> If it's the former, though, it could be very interesting to explore how someone who on the surface <i>seems</i> to be out of sync with the Chorus's beliefs is actually very much <i>in</i> sync with them, and maybe even <i>exemplifies</i> the Tradition's ideals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T19:40:25-07:00","id":1463776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463641-would-it-be-impossible-to-play-a-chorister-polytheist?p=1463775#post1463775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you want to play something like that, you should put some serious thought into whether the Celestial Chorus is the right faction for your character, and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a serious consideration, not only for the Chorus. Most characters don't need it but will be better explored when you put some thought in why they're going to be of a given Tradition, because almost every Paradigm can actually be folded into more than one of them. But subversive expectations must be especially considered because putting a character that have nothing to do with it in a given Tradition won't be good for anyone involved.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the opposite may provide drama. A character that seems a fit in the surface, but actually identifies with the idea of another Tradition may go through some interesting conflicts, internal and external, and there are many ways to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T19:55:48-07:00","id":1463778,"title":"","content":"And, of course, M20 has heavily revised the notion of the Orphan to not only allow for, but actively <i>encourage</i>, mages with deep and complex paradigms and practices but who aren't aligned with <i>any</i> of the Ascension War factions. So yeah; these days, there's little demand to align with a faction <i>just</i> because of your approach to magick: unlike earlier editions, you shouldn't go Chorister for the paradigm; you should go Chorister for the culture and politics. And yes, paradigm is a factor in a given faction's culture; but it's just <i>one</i> factor, and one that can easily be satisfied in other ways \u2014 <i>especially</i> if your intended Focus is on the fringes of a given Tradition's Focus, as would be the case for a polytheistic belief system in the Chorus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T20:16:22-07:00","id":1464680,"title":"","content":"I have played Hindu Choirsters so I definitely think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T18:25:56-07:00","id":1464947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463641-would-it-be-impossible-to-play-a-chorister-polytheist?p=1464680#post1464680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have played Hindu Choirsters so I definitely think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. One of the premade character templates from the original Tradition book was a Hindu, and both that book and others discuss Hinduism within the Chorus. There's also been mention of Santeria practitioners, Incan, and IIRC Wiccan Chorus members. <br /> <br /> From a purely technical prespective, the Chorus are something of a Gnostic mystery cult, in which there are secret hidden truths revealed to those who've been initiated. In this case, the idea that God, Allah, the Hindu Trimurti, the Zoroastrian Ahura Mazda, the Yoruba/Santeria Olodumare, the Wiccan Great Goddess, the Algonquian Gitche Manitou, etc. are all masks/incarnations/what have you of The One, the secret &quot;true&quot; divinity of light and creation that created reality and which all mundane human religions are striving to reconnect with. (In this context, beings like St. Michael Archangel, the Zoroastrian god Mithra, the Thunderbird, Garuda, the oricha Yemaja, and so forth are extremely powerful spirits - akin to Celestines and Incarna in Werewolf - in service to The One.)<br /> Back in the old days, this probably also included the likes of New Kingdom Egypt's Amun-Ra (and the Atenism heresy), and the early periods of the Bronze Age Greek religions where Zeus was still held as a sun god. You may very well have had Hellenistic era proto-Chorus groups trying to advocate worship of Zeus Ammon as a path to creating a unifying faith for the post-Alexander world. (My own head canon has been that the Sisters of Gabrielle probably started as a sect devoted to Apollo in his role as averter of evil, protector of youth, and god of healing and prophecy, even if they've been recruiting from Christians, Jews, Muslims, and others for the past few millennia.) <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T18:34:52-07:00","id":1464949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463641-would-it-be-impossible-to-play-a-chorister-polytheist?p=1464947#post1464947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. One of the premade character templates from the original Tradition book was a Hindu, and both that book and others discuss Hinduism within the Chorus. There's also been mention of Santeria practitioners, Incan, and IIRC Wiccan Chorus members.<br /> <br /> From a purely technical prespective, the Chorus are something of a Gnostic mystery cult, in which there are secret hidden truths revealed to those who've been initiated. In this case, the idea that God, Allah, the Hindu Trimurti, the Zoroastrian Ahura Mazda, the Yoruba/Santeria Olodumare, the Wiccan Great Goddess, the Algonquian Gitche Manitou, etc. are all masks/incarnations/what have you of The One, the secret &quot;true&quot; divinity of light and creation that created reality and which all mundane human religions are striving to reconnect with. (In this context, beings like St. Michael Archangel, the Zoroastrian god Mithra, the Thunderbird, Garuda, the oricha Yemaja, and so forth are extremely powerful spirits - akin to Celestines and Incarna in Werewolf - in service to The One.)<br /> Back in the old days, this probably also included the likes of New Kingdom Egypt's Amun-Ra (and the Atenism heresy), and the early periods of the Bronze Age Greek religions where Zeus was still held as a sun god. You may very well have had Hellenistic era proto-Chorus groups trying to advocate worship of Zeus Ammon as a path to creating a unifying faith for the post-Alexander world. (My own head canon has been that the Sisters of Gabrielle probably started as a sect devoted to Apollo in his role as averter of evil, protector of youth, and god of healing and prophecy, even if they've been recruiting from Christians, Jews, Muslims, and others for the past few millennia.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the simplest terms, Choirsters believe there are many roads to God and have a lot of definitive evidence to that regard. Tolerance is pretty much baked into their Paradigm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T19:05:41-07:00","id":1464952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463641-would-it-be-impossible-to-play-a-chorister-polytheist?p=1464947#post1464947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. One of the premade character templates from the original Tradition book was a Hindu, and both that book and others discuss Hinduism within the Chorus. There's also been mention of Santeria practitioners, Incan, and IIRC Wiccan Chorus members. <br /> <br /> From a purely technical prespective, the Chorus are something of a Gnostic mystery cult, in which there are secret hidden truths revealed to those who've been initiated. In this case, the idea that God, Allah, the Hindu Trimurti, the Zoroastrian Ahura Mazda, the Yoruba/Santeria Olodumare, the Wiccan Great Goddess, the Algonquian Gitche Manitou, etc. are all masks/incarnations/what have you of The One, the secret &amp;quot;true&amp;quot; divinity of light and creation that created reality and which all mundane human religions are striving to reconnect with. (In this context, beings like St. Michael Archangel, the Zoroastrian god Mithra, the Thunderbird, Garuda, the oricha Yemaja, and so forth are extremely powerful spirits - akin to Celestines and Incarna in Werewolf - in service to The One.)<br /> Back in the old days, this probably also included the likes of New Kingdom Egypt's Amun-Ra (and the Atenism heresy), and the early periods of the Bronze Age Greek religions where Zeus was still held as a sun god. You may very well have had Hellenistic era proto-Chorus groups trying to advocate worship of Zeus Ammon as a path to creating a unifying faith for the post-Alexander world. (My own head canon has been that the Sisters of Gabrielle probably started as a sect devoted to Apollo in his role as averter of evil, protector of youth, and god of healing and prophecy, even if they've been recruiting from Christians, Jews, Muslims, and others for the past few millennia.) <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The only quibble I have with this is that the Celestial Chorus isn't that old; it didn't exist before the 1400s. That said, you can count all of the groups that No One of Consequence mentioned as its forebears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}